---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="SkanPay - QR Checkout Gateway"
  description="SkanPay helps merchants and payment partners coordinate QR checkout requests, customer approval, coupon or voucher logic, and merchant-readable results."
  activePath="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">QR payment gateway</p>
      <h1>Make QR checkout clear enough to trust</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        SkanPay helps merchants and payment partners turn a scan into a structured checkout request: customer approval, optional coupon or voucher logic, and a result staff can read.
      </p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Contact SkanPay</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/beamcash-demo/">View BeamCash</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-check-list" aria-label="SkanPay checkout priorities">
        <span>Merchant sees checkout status</span>
        <span>Customer confirms the request</span>
        <span>Partners get a defined handoff</span>
      </div>
      <div class="trust-strip" aria-label="SkanPay focus areas">
        <div class="trust-item">
          <strong>01</strong>
          Request
        </div>
        <div class="trust-item">
          <strong>02</strong>
          Approval
        </div>
        <div class="trust-item">
          <strong>03</strong>
          Result
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-panel" aria-label="SkanPay platform overview">
      <div class="panel-header">
        <span>Checkout state model</span>
        <strong>Scan to result</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="system-card">
        <div>
          <span>Request</span>
          <strong>Amount, merchant reference, session details</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Scan</span>
          <strong>Customer opens a clear checkout prompt</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Decision</span>
          <strong>Approval, redemption, or cancellation state</strong>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span>Merchant result</span>
          <strong>Confirmed, redeemed, cancelled, or expired</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="signal-grid">
        <div><span>Audience</span><strong>Merchants</strong></div>
        <div><span>Partners</span><strong>Wallets</strong></div>
        <div><span>Logic</span><strong>Offers</strong></div>
        <div><span>Scope</span><strong>Gateway</strong></div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pain points</p>
        <h2>A QR code is easy. The checkout state is the hard part.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        SkanPay focuses on the operating layer between the store, customer, payment app, and redemption logic.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pain-grid compact-grid">
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Staff</span>
        <h3>Unclear status slows checkout</h3>
        <p>Staff need to know whether a request was scanned, approved, cancelled, expired, or completed.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Customer</span>
        <h3>Trust depends on context</h3>
        <p>The customer should see who they are paying, what they are approving, and what happens next.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Offers</span>
        <h3>Coupons need coordination</h3>
        <p>Coupon or voucher value has to be validated without becoming a separate staff process.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="pain-card">
        <span>Partners</span>
        <h3>Each system needs a role</h3>
        <p>Wallet, payment, loyalty, and merchant systems need a defined checkout boundary.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section technical-band">
    <div class="process-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>Four states make the flow readable</h2>
        <p class="section-intro">
          The model is simple enough to explain in a meeting, but structured enough for technical integration planning.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="homepage-flow-grid" aria-label="SkanPay checkout flow">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Create request</h3>
          <p>The merchant starts a QR checkout request with amount, merchant reference, and session details.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Customer scans</h3>
          <p>The customer opens a checkout prompt and reviews the request before approving.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Coordinate logic</h3>
          <p>Payment, wallet, coupon, or voucher rules can be evaluated in the checkout handoff.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Return result</h3>
          <p>The merchant receives a readable state such as confirmed, redeemed, cancelled, or expired.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section demo-preview">
    <div class="demo-preview-copy">
      <img class="beamcash-wordmark" src="/beamcash/beamcash-wordmark.svg" alt="BeamCash" />
      <p class="eyebrow">Demo app under SkanPay</p>
      <h2>BeamCash turns the QR concept into a product demo</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">
        BeamCash is the working app-style demo used to show seller setup, QR display, and buyer approval before a deeper SkanPay integration conversation.
      </p>
      <div class="mini-flow-list" aria-label="BeamCash demo flow">
        <span>Set up seller</span>
        <span>Display QR</span>
        <span>Review checkout</span>
      </div>
      <a class="button primary" href="/beamcash-demo/">View Demo</a>
    </div>
    <div class="demo-screens" aria-label="BeamCash demo screens">
      <figure>
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-seller-dashboard-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash seller dashboard with QR code" />
        <figcaption>Seller QR dashboard</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/beamcash/beamcash-buyer-checkout-mobile.png" alt="BeamCash buyer checkout screen" />
        <figcaption>Buyer checkout</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section homepage-faq">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
        <h2>What partners usually ask first</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Short answers for merchants and payment partners evaluating the QR checkout model.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details>
        <summary>What does SkanPay do?</summary>
        <p>SkanPay is focused on QR checkout coordination: request creation, customer approval, optional redemption logic, and merchant-readable results.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is SkanPay replacing existing processors?</summary>
        <p>SkanPay is presented as a gateway and coordination layer. Processor or acquirer details depend on the integration model.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why show BeamCash?</summary>
        <p>BeamCash gives partners a concrete demo of seller setup, QR display, and customer checkout approval.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Next step</p>
      <h2>Bring QR payment conversations into focus.</h2>
      <p>Share the merchant, partner, or product details you want SkanPay to support and the team can follow up directly.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Start a Conversation</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
